    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>1.Midterm examination 30%, 2.&nbsp;Final presentation 40%, 3.&nbsp;Report on gained knowledge 20%, 4.&nbsp;Attendances 10%</div>\n",
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "- Students are expected to attend class on time. Unless you are ill or facing an emergency, you should arrive before class begins. If you must leave early for any reason, please inform the instructor in advance.\n- All students should treat others with respect and conduct themselves in a reasonable, responsible, and courteous manner at all times.\n- Talking, reading, sleeping, or working on unrelated assignments during class is not permitted. Side conversations should be minimized except during designated group discussions.\n- When classmates are presenting or asking questions, you should listen attentively. When you are presenting, speak clearly and face your group or the entire class so that everyone can hear you.\n- Laptops, tablets, and similar devices may be used for taking notes. Otherwise, they should be put away.\n- Mobile phones, PDAs, and other electronic devices must be turned off or set to silent mode during class and kept out of use.\n- Wearing headphones in class is not allowed.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "Students are expected to complete all learning tasks according to the course schedule, participate actively and responsibly in all learning activities, and submit assignments on time. Students who fulfill the course requirements and achieve the intended learning outcomes will receive the grades they deserve.\nIf you encounter difficulties in your learning during the semester, you are encouraged to make use of the instructor’s office hours or arrange an alternative meeting time to discuss possible solutions and improvement strategies together.",
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div><!--StartFragment -->\n<div>Students are expected to uphold the highest standards of academic integrity. The following behaviors constitute academic misconduct:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Submitting work that is wholly or partially created by someone else.</li>\n\t<li>Copying, plagiarizing, or using unauthorized materials in assignments, quizzes, or examinations.</li>\n\t<li>Allowing others to copy one&rsquo;s work or assisting others in dishonest behavior.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div>Violations will result in a grade of zero for the specific assignment, quiz, or examination. Repeated offenses will be processed according to the <em>Feng Chia University Student Rewards and Penalties Regulations</em>.</div>\n<!--EndFragment --></div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
